The code snippet above checks if the count before and after inserting an item in the ArrayList remains the same. If the count is not the same, it means that the insert operation did not correctly update the count of the ArrayList.

```cs
Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListCount == New_arrListCount + 1, "Count before and after insert should remain same");
Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListIndexOfX < Old_arrListCount, "Index of x before adding x is -1");
Assert.IsTrue(Old_arrListIndexOfX >= 0, "Index of x before adding x should be greater than or equal to 0");
Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListIndexOfX == Old_arrListCount, "Index of x after adding x should be count of the array list");
```

The code snippet above checks if the count before and after inserting an item in the ArrayList remains the same and if the index of the item before adding the item is -1 and the index of the item after adding the item is equal to the count of the ArrayList. If any of these conditions are not met, it means that the insert operation did not correctly update the index and count of the ArrayList.

